# Accessibility (SPOTS)

All UI the agent writes or changes must be keyboard- and screen-reader accessible. Inaccessible UI blocks kids, caregivers, and symptom reporting.

**Target:** WCAG 2.1 AA — `app/_lib/testing/a11y.ts`, `.github/workflows/a11y.yml`.

## Non-negotiables
- Semantic HTML first (`button`, `a`, `input`, `label`, landmarks) before ARIA/custom widgets
- Full keyboard use: focus visible, logical tab order, no traps (except modals with Escape/close)
- Every control has an accessible name; announce important state changes; hide decorative content from AT
- Never color-only cues; icon-only controls need `aria-label` (or equivalent)
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` when adding animation

## Structure & names
- One `<h1>` per page/view; don’t skip heading levels
- Main landmark: `#main-content` (see `app/_lib/utils/focus-a11y.ts`); keep skip-to-main
- Labels on every input (visible `<label>` or `aria-label` / `aria-labelledby`); meaningful `alt` (decorative: `alt=""`)
- Dialogs: `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, labelled; trap focus; restore focus on close; background inert via focus-a11y helpers
- Live regions for loading/errors/view changes (`aria-live`); prefer visible text over redundant ARIA

## Keyboard, forms, tests
- Reuse `app/_lib/hooks/a11y/` (e.g. `useRadioGroupKeyboard`) and `useFocusOnViewEnter` / focus helpers for route/view enter and overlays
- Wire field errors with `aria-invalid` + `aria-describedby`; use `aria-busy` when content is replacing
- New/changed UI: add or update `*.a11y.test.tsx` with `expectNoA11yViolations`; do not disable `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` without team approval
- Flag what JSDOM can’t verify (e.g. contrast) for manual VoiceOver/NVDA review

## SPOTS-specific
- Symptom flows (cart, questions, body map, Problem Station): selection, progress, and destructive actions must be named and keyboard-operable
- Don’t put extra PHI in `aria-label` beyond what’s already visible/appropriate for the role
- Pediatric tone in accessible names — align with healthcare requirements

## Reject
- `<div onClick>` without role, keyboard support, and name
- `tabIndex={0}` on non-interactive elements to fake controls
- `aria-hidden="true"` on focusable or essential content
- Placeholder-only “labels”; removing skip link or `#main-content`
